WEBVTT

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.090
Wow!

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:10.730
Hey!

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.760
Quit slackin’ and keep to yer posts!

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.680
It wouldn’t hurt if
we watched a little!

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.740
Please, Shinpatsu!

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.350
My, that was a great bout!

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.360
It was the match of a lifetime!

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.320
Man, I missed the best part!

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.360
This has truly been a
success, has it not?

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.300
This should substantially add
to the Roshigumi’s funds.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.520
Yeah, but seeing everyone happy
like this is what matters most.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.600
So, that a wrap?

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:23.990
We’re heading back!

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.200
Commander!

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.980
I wish to report something immediately.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.440
Hey, guys! We’re going!

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.300
What’s the problem?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.410
Serizawa-san has done it yet again.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:52.270
The Brightly Burning Beacon

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.280
What in the...?!

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.410
Took you long enough.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.690
Were you having fun with that sumo
demonstration or whatever?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.520
Serizawa-san, was this your doing?

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.950
The Yamato Store wrongfully

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.040
gained its fortune by
trading with foreigners.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.430
This is a corrupt merchant.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.970
There is also suspicion that he was
giving money to some ronin.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.030
Suspicion?

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.390
Furthermore, he refused
to financially help us.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.440
It is only natural that he be punished.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:39.190
In short, you’re lashing out because
he wouldn’t lend you money?

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.350
Hey, put that fire out ASAP!

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:41.950
S-Sir!

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.050
Wait!

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.700
What do you think you’re doing?

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.730
There was no need to set the place

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.600
ablaze if you lacked hard evidence!

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.200
Hijikata, are you implying that I,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.670
our highest-ranked officer as chief,

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.210
would fabricate a story?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.830
Search the inside of that warehouse!

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.710
We may find some evidence.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.610
Very well.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.430
They’re no different
from those rogue samurai.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.620
They really are a nuisance!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.620
Now they even burn down stores?

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.440
Damn Wolves of Mibu!

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.120
Let it go, Ibuki.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.980
Why?! Aren’t you pissed?

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.740
Right now we should focus
on the problem before us.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.270
No matter how long you stay,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.960
you aren’t getting any money.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.290
Why don’t you go back to Hishiya?

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.930
I have nowhere to go back to.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.880
My husband kicked me out

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.780
with nothing but what I had on me.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.190
Life for a mistress is
wretched, isn’t it?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.710
You intend to kill me?

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.310
Wh-whatever could you mean?

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.970
If you spend a life next to death,

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.820
you can easily pick up on
someone’s killing intent.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.020
If you have nowhere
else to go, stay here.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.340
You could kill me at any
time if you stay by my side.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.870
You are a difficult man to understand.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.790
We are here to report what we

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.550
learned about yesterday’s incident.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.220
Due to profiting from
trade with foreigners,

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.990
Note: The Tenchugumi were a
group of Imperial Nationalists.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.990
the Tenchugumi had their
eyes set on that shop.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.540
So the shop owner paid

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.750
national imperialistic
ronin to serve as hired guards.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.960
Meaning there was some truth in
what Serizawa-san said, eh?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.010
Honestly, both sides have their points.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.660
But all that the people
of Kyoto will remember

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.800
is the fact that the Mibu
Roshigumi burnt that building.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.570
As things stand, isn’t it simply a

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.250
repeat of a past offense, Commander?

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.370
To hear that coming from you,

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.580
this must not sit well with you at all.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.230
You have my apologies.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.260
I spoke out of line.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.280
Hajime-kun is right.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.780
That man really is a nuisance.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.040
At any rate,

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:21.190
we’ll have to rake up the merits,
no matter how small.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.070
Master, shouldn’t you
slow down a little?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.070
Keep it coming!

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.780
S-sir...

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.260
Even drinking isn’t helping...

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:48.190
I went and asked for more saké.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.440
Serizawa-san?!

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.030
Master!

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.700
Are you okay?!

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.010
Serizawa-san!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:02.910
Who...

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:05.710
...are you?

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.210
Where am I?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.240
What am I doing here?

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.720
M-master, are you all right?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.560
Calm down!

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.200
You’ve had too much
to drink, haven’t you?

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.840
I’m Ibuki!

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.040
Don’t you recognize me, Serizawa-san?

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.820
I could hardly remember the face
of each and every cur I see.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.500
Sheesh! Dumb drunk!

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.170
Serizawa-sama, is something the matter?

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:51.280
Yer bein’ too loud!

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.510
What’s all the ruckus?

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.760
Hey! Ain’t you Serizawa
from the Wolves of Mibu?!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.510
What?!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.020
And what if I am?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.700
Do you think you could kill me?

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.470
If so, I’ll take you on.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.280
I wouldn’t.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.530
You are hardly a match for him.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.680
Come along! Go right this way.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.570
I shall prepare another room for you.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.780
You’re suffering from
a disease, are you not?

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.950
Most of your body should
have been rendered useless.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.590
It’s a miracle you can even stand.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.560
I’m impressed you could
tell upon first meeting me.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.970
I have seen someone inflicted
with the same disease.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.430
He became unable to remember
who he was or recognize others.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:59.070
He endured suffering, then died.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:04.080
Before too long, you
shall face the same fate.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.020
What of it?

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.300
I am well aware that I will
writhe in agony as I die.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.050
In fact, that’s what I want.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:22.350
Lowly human, you are rather intriguing.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:34.700
This is medicine to
suppress their bloodlust.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.270
I will continue to modify the
elixir, but use this for now.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.180
Oh, I appreciate it!

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.250
Now that I have this,

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.890
those monsters
should be easier to manage.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.000
Assuming all goes as planned...

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.340
But you must actually
administer the medicine

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.710
and discern its effectiveness.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:57.260
Yes, I am well aware.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.530
Headquarters of the Kyoto Military Commissioner
Konkaikoumyouji Main Temple

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.520
Raise your heads.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.630
The lord holds your work with the

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.840
Mibu Roshigumi in high regard.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.350
It is an honor to hear that.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:19.310
But, nonetheless, some of Serizawa’s

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.530
recent antics cannot be overlooked.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.250
I feel fully responsible
for such failings.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.030
You have my humblest apologies.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.530
Devise a plan to deal with him...

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:30.790
...before he sullies the Aizu name.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:31.680
Sir!

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.390
What was that?!

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.750
You’re all here?

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.240
Of course we are!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:05.200
We heard that
outrageously loud noise.

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.950
The roar of artillery seems to have
come from the Imperial Palace.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.720
Say, shouldn’t we be
headin’ over there?

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.200
No, Aizu has not yet issued
orders for us to mobilize.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:20.960
We should avoid acting on our own.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.970
Yamazaki and Shimada have
already left to investigate.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.500
We’re on standby until
we receive their reports.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:34.480
What?!

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:38.730
Aizu and Satsuma are
guarding the Sakaimachi Gate?

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.580
What?!

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:45.890
I believe Choshu originally
guarded that post.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.790
Right.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.320
The Choshu Domain is looking
for a chance

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.000
to enter the palace,

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.470
but Aizu and Satsuma
are staring them down,

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.460
intent not to let them step foot inside.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.290
The situation is volatile.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.500
Battle could break out at any moment.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.010
Battle, huh?

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:10.910
But why are the feuding Aizu and
Satsuma Domains teaming up?

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:13.610
It is beyond me.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.490
It merely means that the world is not as

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.770
simple as you simple-minded louts.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.280
What was that?!

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.680
Both Satsuma and Aizu have

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.890
shunned Choshu because of
how they enter and leave

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:32.460
the Imperial Court as
if it were their own.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.710
Clashing ideals is a minor problem

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.260
before the chance to crush Choshu.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.290
Thanks for the lecture.

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:44.210
I don’t care about what’s
in the minds of opportunists

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.020
who change their attitudes
based on the situation.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.250
So? What should we do?

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.710
We cannot move the squad without

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:55.310
orders from the Aizu Domain.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.310
So we have to wait?

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.620
We’re leaving!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.260
We’ll merely lose the chance

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:10.820
to earn distinction if we sit around!

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.840
I bring orders!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:27.160
The Roshigumi are to hurry
to the Imperial Palace!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.700
Guard the gates!

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:35.410
Our lord has given the order!

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.850
The Mibu Roshigumi are to mobilize!

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.960
We shall be the ones
to protect the emperor!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.540
Yeah!

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.860
Truth

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.370
Truth

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.270
Who goes there?

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:02.200
This is a gate to the
revered Imperial Palace.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.880
Rogue warriors, leave
with all due haste!

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:09.140
We are the Mibu Roshigumi,
who serve under

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.860
Lt. General Matsudaira.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.890
We came here under official orders.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.240
The Mibu Roshigumi?

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:20.190
I’ve never heard that name before.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.760
Leave at once!

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.270
What?!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.360
What gives?

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.870
We still lack a name.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:29.540
I imagine there are some in the

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.110
domain who do not know of us.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:34.280
I am sorry to inconvenience you,

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.920
but could you go check with the officials?

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.060
Bug off!

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:40.210
We never received any orders about you!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.670
Leave immediately!

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:51.180
He said to go confirm your
orders with the officials right now!

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:52.890
Wh-why you...!

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.180
Since you have directed
that spear at me,

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.210
you must be prepared to get cut down

00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.400
and killed within an instant, yes?

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:06.460
I am the loyal and patriotic samurai,

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.100
Kamo Serizawa!

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:11.390
I command the Mibu Roshigumi
that serves the Aizu Domain

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:13.660
and you WILL let us enter the palace!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:27.030
Such a fuss over the
Choshu Domain alone?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.710
The Shogunate’s authority
has certainly fallen.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.610
Does this mean the times are changing?

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.850
Inoue-san, how’s everyone?

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.350
They carried out their
duty safe and sound.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:47.860
That right?

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.220
Thank goodness!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.360
Could you help me prepare for supper?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:54.540
Sure!

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:02.390
Everyone, you did
wonderfully the other day.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:06.500
The Lord of Aizu was most
impressed by our work.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.040
He now says that he would like

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.880
to officially entrust
patrolling Kyoto to us.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.530
Wow, that’s awesome!

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:16.890
This should make conducting
our patrols a lot easier!

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.610
And he bestowed a great honor upon us!

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:23.410
The Lord of Aizu has bequeathed
a new name to our squad.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:25.890
Shinsengumi

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:26.920
Shin-

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:27.920
-sen-

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.400
-gumi

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.350
We’re the Shinsengumi!

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.830
The Shinsengumi...

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.820
This name used to be the name of

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.790
an actual organization
in the Aizu Domain.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.410
Those who excelled in military
arts gathered under it.

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.760
That’s kinda inspiring, isn’t it?

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:48.920
Yeah!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.920
So, in other words,

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.430
the Lord of Aizu
believes that the Roshigumi

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.530
are worthy as warriors
to inherit that name.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:03.380
To meet his expectations,

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:06.060
we must further
dedicate ourselves to our mission!

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.260
Yeah!

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.300
It’s not often you get
a day as good as today!

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:15.140
Hijikata-san, how ’bout it?
It’s been ages since we partied!

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:20.200
Yeah. We’ll all celebrate tonight.

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.430
That’s what I wanted to hear!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.210
In Service of Matsudaira, Defender of Higo:
Shinsengumi

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:32.210
Those newly selected, huh?

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.950
Saito? What’re you doing there?

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.220
Ibuki?

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:43.490
Didn’t he say that those
skilled in military arts

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.700
gathered under this distinguished name?

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:49.230
Indeed. I never so much as imagined that

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.750
I would someday serve as a warrior

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.070
under a name such as this.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.870
Really? I’d say you’re good enough,

00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:59.200
considering your swordsmanship.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.030
Once already, I have abandoned
the way of the sword.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.490
Huh? What do you mean?

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:12.010
I did so, anguished that I could not
follow the way of the warrior.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:17.570
But even so, the Roshigumi
welcomed me back once more.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.680
I don my sword yet again...

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:26.680
As such, my resolution is strong.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.540
This time, I WILL persevere
and live as a warrior!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.310
Hey, you two!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:37.360
The party’s gonna start!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.320
Hurry and join us.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.470
Let’s go.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:41.520
Yeah.

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.270
So this is where you went, Kondou-san!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.570
Yeah, I needed to get some air.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.470
It ain’t easy hanging out
with a bunch of heavy drinkers.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.160
We’ve finally come this far!

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:09.600
I feel as if all of
our work has paid off.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:13.250
Yeah, but it’s too soon to let up.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.050
The goals we are striving
for are still a ways off.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.570
Indeed, they are...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.080
If everyone’s hearts join as one under

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.620
the name of the Shinsengumi,

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.120
the day we realize our ideals
will definitely come!

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:31.120
That is what I believe.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.070
Yeah.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.070
Same here.

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:50.060
Their party seems to have
grown rather lively.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.180
The Aizu will take them in now.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:58.390
From here out, they will be forced

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:00.510
to stomp on several of
their sacred images.

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:02.150
Sacred images?

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.420
Their sacred images of a warrior.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.580
They must not balk at
dirtying their own hands

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.250
and cross over trials they
do not wish to endure.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:19.730
It’s a matter of whether or
not they can become... devils.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.170
It hurts!

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.690
Hurry and set me free!

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.200
Be quiet!

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.790
Don’t you want to become

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:47.640
full-fledged furies as soon as possible?

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:30.450
It is necessary for us to investigate
whether the secret about

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:32.340
the Water of Life has been leaked.

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.620
This is the power of a fury!

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:36.640
The new era will be handed over to

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:38.490
whosoever possesses this medicine!

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.660
Is that all you have to say?

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.020
A Moonlit Night Filled
with Flowers
